module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.AdmissibleDominating
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.StrictTransform.AffineChartExceptionalPreimage
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.StrictTransform.AffineChartExistence
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.StrictTransform.QuotientModelChart

/-!
# The chart of a base change over a blowup chart, in the quotient model

[Stacks, Tag 0810] is proved at the scheme level as
`Stacks.StrictTransform.exists_fg_ideal_forall_chartFreeOfRank`, whose conclusion is the
*universally quantified* predicate `Stacks.StrictTransform.ChartFreeOfRank`: it speaks about every
affine chart `j : Spec B ⟶ X ×_S Y` of a base change on which the inverse image of the centre is
the zero locus of the image of the chart's denominator, and claims nothing about the existence of
such a chart. This file produces the charts, for `Y = Bl_ℐ(S)` with `S` affine, so that the
predicate becomes usable.

The chart is the one of `Stacks.StrictTransform.affineBaseChangeChartMap` over the blowup chart
`Stacks.Blowup.blowUpQuotientChart`, and its source is the spectrum of
`Γ(X, ⊤) ⊗_{Γ(S, ⊤)} Γ(S, ⊤)[ℐ(⊤)/a]` with the second factor in the quotient model — which is the
ring `ChartFreeOfRank` is instantiated at by `exists_fg_ideal_forall_chartFreeOfRank`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.StrictTransform.blowUpQuotientChartOfIdeal`: the blowup chart in the quotient model, as
  a chart of `AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp` rather than of `Stacks.Blowup.blowUp`.
* `Stacks.StrictTransform.blowUpQuotientBaseChangeChart`: the chart
  `Spec (Γ(X, ⊤) ⊗_{Γ(S, ⊤)} Γ(S, ⊤)[ℐ(⊤)/a]) ⟶ X ×_S Bl_ℐ(S)`.

## Main results

* `Ideal.map_algebraMap_tensorProduct_eq_span_of_map_eq_span`: an ideal whose extension to `T` is
  principal has principal extension to `A ⊗_R T`, generated by the image of the same element.
* `Stacks.StrictTransform.blowUpQuotientChartOfIdeal_blowUpToBase_isoSpec`: the hypothesis `hc` of
  `Stacks.StrictTransform.affineBaseChangeChartMap` for the blowup chart over an affine base.
* `Stacks.StrictTransform.isOpenImmersion_blowUpQuotientBaseChangeChart`,
  `Stacks.StrictTransform.blowUpQuotientBaseChangeChart_fst` and
  `Stacks.StrictTransform.blowUpQuotientBaseChangeChart_snd`: the chart is an open immersion, it
  induces the structure map of the tensor product on `X` — which is the hypothesis `hfst` of
  `Stacks.StrictTransform.ChartFreeOfRank` — and it lies over the blowup chart.
* `Stacks.StrictTransform.preimage_exceptionalPreimage_blowUpQuotientBaseChangeChart`: the
  hypothesis `hZ` of `Stacks.StrictTransform.ChartFreeOfRank` for this chart, with `β` the image
  of `a`.
* `Stacks.StrictTransform.exists_blowUpQuotientChartOfIdeal_preimage`: the blowup charts cover the
  blowup of an affine scheme.

## Implementation notes

The repository has two constructions of the blowup: `Stacks.Blowup.blowUp`, which admissibility
and the charts of [Stacks, Tag 0804] are phrased with, and `AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp`, which the
strict transform of [Stacks, Tag 080D] and the statement of [Stacks, Tag 0811] are phrased with.
`Stacks.Blowup.blowUpQuotientChart` is a chart of the first, so everything here is stated for the
second and the passage is `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpIso` together with
`Stacks.Blowup.blowUpIso_hom_comp`, which identifies them over the base.

The hypothesis `hc` of `Stacks.StrictTransform.affineBaseChangeChartMap` is
`Stacks.Blowup.blowUpQuotientChart_blowUpToBase` at the affine open `⊤`, where
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.fromSpec_top` turns the inclusion of that open into
`S.isoSpec.inv` and cancels it.

The hypothesis `hZ` is `Stacks.StrictTransform.preimage_exceptionalPreimage_eq_principalZeroLocus`,
whose ideal-theoretic input is [Stacks, Tag 07Z3] part (2) — `blowup_idealMap_eq_span`, that the
centre becomes principal on the chart of the blowup — pushed along
`Γ(S, ⊤)[ℐ(⊤)/a] ⟶ Γ(X, ⊤) ⊗ Γ(S, ⊤)[ℐ(⊤)/a]`. That push is
`Ideal.map_algebraMap_tensorProduct_eq_span_of_map_eq_span`, and it is where the identification of
the generator with the image of `a` under `Γ(S, ⊤) ⟶ Γ(X, ⊤)` happens, through the scalar tower of
the tensor product.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0810](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0810)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0804](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0804)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 080D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/080D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07Z3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07Z3)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Limits AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace
open scoped TensorProduct

universe u

/-- **An ideal that becomes principal in `T` becomes principal in `A ⊗_R T`.** If the extension
of `J ⊆ R` to `T` is generated by `t`, its extension to `A ⊗_R T` is generated by the image of
`t`, because `R ⟶ A ⊗_R T` factors through `T`. -/
public theorem Ideal.map_algebraMap_tensorProduct_eq_span_of_map_eq_span {R A T : Type u}
    [CommRing R] [CommRing A] [CommRing T] [Algebra R A] [Algebra R T] (J : Ideal R) (b : R)
    (hJ : Ideal.map (algebraMap R T) J = Ideal.span {algebraMap R T b}) :
    Ideal.map (algebraMap R (A ⊗[R] T)) J = Ideal.span {algebraMap R (A ⊗[R] T) b} := by
  set φ : T →+* A ⊗[R] T :=
    (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : T →ₐ[R] A ⊗[R] T).toRingHom with hφ
  have hcomp : (algebraMap R (A ⊗[R] T) : R →+* A ⊗[R] T) = φ.comp (algebraMap R T) :=
    RingHom.ext fun r ↦ by simp [hφ]
  have hb : φ (algebraMap R T b) = algebraMap R (A ⊗[R] T) b := (RingHom.congr_fun hcomp b).symm
  conv_lhs => rw [hcomp]
  rw [← Ideal.map_map, hJ, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, hb]

namespace Stacks.StrictTransform

variable {X S : Scheme.{u}} [IsAffine X] [IsAffine S] (f : X ⟶ S) (ℐ : S.IdealSheafData)
  (a : Γ(S, ⊤)) [ha : Fact (a ∈ ℐ.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top S⟩)]

/-- **The blowup chart in the quotient model, for `AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp`.** The charts of
`Stacks.Blowup.blowUpQuotientChart` are charts of `Stacks.Blowup.blowUp`, the construction
admissibility is phrased with; the strict transform of [Stacks, Tag 080D] and the statement of
[Stacks, Tag 0811] are about `AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp`. The two are identified over the base by
`Stacks.Blowup.blowUpIso`, and this is the chart transported along it. -/
public def blowUpQuotientChartOfIdeal :
    Spec (CommRingCat.of (Blowup (ℐ.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top S⟩) a)) ⟶ blowUp ℐ :=
  Stacks.Blowup.blowUpQuotientChart ℐ ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top S⟩ a ≫
    (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpIso ℐ).hom

/-- The transported chart is an open immersion. -/
public instance isOpenImmersion_blowUpQuotientChartOfIdeal :
    IsOpenImmersion (blowUpQuotientChartOfIdeal ℐ a) := by
  unfold blowUpQuotientChartOfIdeal
  infer_instance

/-- **The hypothesis `hc` of a chart of a base change, for the blowup chart of an affine base.**
Over an affine `S` the composite `Spec Γ(S, ⊤)[ℐ(⊤)/a] ⟶ Bl_ℐ(S) ⟶ S`, read through
`S.isoSpec`, is `Spec` of the structure map of the chart ring.

This is `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpQuotientChart_blowUpToBase` at the affine open `⊤`, where the
inclusion of that open is `S.isoSpec.inv`, together with
`Stacks.Blowup.blowUpIso_hom_comp`. -/
public theorem blowUpQuotientChartOfIdeal_blowUpToBase_isoSpec :
    (blowUpQuotientChartOfIdeal ℐ a ≫ blowUpToBase ℐ) ≫ S.isoSpec.hom =
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(S, ⊤)
        (Blowup (ℐ.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top S⟩) a))) := by
  have htop : (Stacks.RelativeProj.isAffineOpen
      (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top S⟩ : S.affineOpens)).fromSpec = S.isoSpec.inv :=
    IsAffineOpen.fromSpec_top
  have h₁ : blowUpQuotientChartOfIdeal ℐ a ≫ blowUpToBase ℐ =
      Stacks.Blowup.blowUpQuotientChart ℐ ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top S⟩ a ≫
        Stacks.Blowup.blowUpToBase ℐ := by
    rw [blowUpQuotientChartOfIdeal, Category.assoc, Stacks.Blowup.blowUpIso_hom_comp]
  rw [h₁, Stacks.Blowup.blowUpQuotientChart_blowUpToBase, Category.assoc, htop, Iso.inv_hom_id,
    Category.comp_id]

/-- **The affine chart of the base change `X ×_S Bl_ℐ(S)` over a blowup chart.** For `X` and `S`
affine and `a ∈ ℐ(⊤)`, this is the chart whose source is the spectrum of
`Γ(X, ⊤) ⊗_{Γ(S, ⊤)} Γ(S, ⊤)[ℐ(⊤)/a]`, with the affine blowup algebra in the quotient model.

It is `Stacks.StrictTransform.affineBaseChangeChartMap` over
`Stacks.Blowup.blowUpQuotientChart`. -/
public def blowUpQuotientBaseChangeChart :
    letI : Algebra Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤) := f.appTop.hom.toAlgebra
    Spec (CommRingCat.of (Γ(X, ⊤) ⊗[Γ(S, ⊤)]
        Blowup (ℐ.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top S⟩) a)) ⟶ baseChange f (blowUpToBase ℐ) :=
  affineBaseChangeChartMap f (blowUpToBase ℐ)
    (Blowup (ℐ.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top S⟩) a)
    (blowUpQuotientChartOfIdeal ℐ a)
    (blowUpQuotientChartOfIdeal_blowUpToBase_isoSpec ℐ a)

/-- The chart of the base change over a blowup chart is an open immersion: the blowup chart is
one. -/
public theorem isOpenImmersion_blowUpQuotientBaseChangeChart :
    IsOpenImmersion (blowUpQuotientBaseChangeChart f ℐ a) :=
  isOpenImmersion_affineBaseChangeChartMap f (blowUpToBase ℐ) _ _ _

/-- **The hypothesis `hfst` of `Stacks.StrictTransform.ChartFreeOfRank` for this chart.** The
composite to `X`, read through `X.isoSpec`, is `Spec` of the structure map
`Γ(X, ⊤) ⟶ Γ(X, ⊤) ⊗_{Γ(S, ⊤)} Γ(S, ⊤)[ℐ(⊤)/a]`. -/
public theorem blowUpQuotientBaseChangeChart_fst :
    letI : Algebra Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤) := f.appTop.hom.toAlgebra
    (blowUpQuotientBaseChangeChart f ℐ a ≫ pullback.fst f (blowUpToBase ℐ)) ≫ X.isoSpec.hom =
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(X, ⊤) (Γ(X, ⊤) ⊗[Γ(S, ⊤)]
        Blowup (ℐ.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top S⟩) a))) :=
  affineBaseChangeChartMap_fst f (blowUpToBase ℐ) _ _ _

/-- The chart of the base change lies over the blowup chart it was built from. -/
public theorem blowUpQuotientBaseChangeChart_snd :
    letI : Algebra Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤) := f.appTop.hom.toAlgebra
    blowUpQuotientBaseChangeChart f ℐ a ≫ pullback.snd f (blowUpToBase ℐ) =
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight :
          Blowup (ℐ.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top S⟩) a →ₐ[Γ(S, ⊤)]
            Γ(X, ⊤) ⊗[Γ(S, ⊤)] Blowup (ℐ.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top S⟩) a).toRingHom) ≫
        blowUpQuotientChartOfIdeal ℐ a :=
  affineBaseChangeChartMap_snd f (blowUpToBase ℐ) _ _ _

/-- **The hypothesis `hZ` of `Stacks.StrictTransform.ChartFreeOfRank` for this chart.** The
inverse image under the chart of `pr_{Bl}^{-1}(Supp (exceptionalIdeal ℐ))` is the zero locus of
the image of `a` in `Γ(X, ⊤) ⊗_{Γ(S, ⊤)} Γ(S, ⊤)[ℐ(⊤)/a]`.

The centre becomes the principal ideal of the image of `a` on the chart of the blowup by
[Stacks, Tag 07Z3] part (2), and that stays principal after tensoring with `Γ(X, ⊤)` by
`Ideal.map_algebraMap_tensorProduct_eq_span_of_map_eq_span`; the conversion of the ideal identity
into the identity of subsets is
`Stacks.StrictTransform.preimage_exceptionalPreimage_eq_principalZeroLocus`. -/
public theorem preimage_exceptionalPreimage_blowUpQuotientBaseChangeChart :
    letI : Algebra Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤) := f.appTop.hom.toAlgebra
    (blowUpQuotientBaseChangeChart f ℐ a).base ⁻¹'
        exceptionalPreimage f (blowUpToBase ℐ) (exceptionalIdeal ℐ) =
      principalZeroLocus (CommRingCat.of (Γ(X, ⊤) ⊗[Γ(S, ⊤)]
          Blowup (ℐ.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top S⟩) a))
        (algebraMap Γ(X, ⊤) (Γ(X, ⊤) ⊗[Γ(S, ⊤)]
          Blowup (ℐ.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top S⟩) a) (f.appTop.hom a)) := by
  let : Algebra Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤) := f.appTop.hom.toAlgebra
  set T := Blowup (ℐ.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top S⟩) a
  set B := Γ(X, ⊤) ⊗[Γ(S, ⊤)] T
  -- the chart lies over `S` through the structure map of `B`
  have hbase : ((blowUpQuotientBaseChangeChart f ℐ a ≫ pullback.fst f (blowUpToBase ℐ) ≫ f))
      ≫ S.isoSpec.hom = Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(S, ⊤) B)) := by
    have he : CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤)) = f.appTop := rfl
    calc ((blowUpQuotientBaseChangeChart f ℐ a ≫ pullback.fst f (blowUpToBase ℐ) ≫ f))
          ≫ S.isoSpec.hom
        = ((blowUpQuotientBaseChangeChart f ℐ a ≫ pullback.fst f (blowUpToBase ℐ))
            ≫ X.isoSpec.hom) ≫ Spec.map f.appTop := by
          simp only [Category.assoc, Scheme.isoSpec_hom_naturality]
      _ = Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(X, ⊤) B)) ≫ Spec.map f.appTop := by
          rw [blowUpQuotientBaseChangeChart_fst f ℐ a]
      _ = Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(S, ⊤) B)) := by
          rw [← he, ← Spec.map_comp]
          congr 1
  -- the centre is principal on the chart
  have hI : Ideal.map (algebraMap Γ(S, ⊤) B) (ℐ.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top S⟩) =
      Ideal.span {algebraMap Γ(X, ⊤) B (f.appTop.hom a)} := by
    have hgen : algebraMap Γ(X, ⊤) B (f.appTop.hom a) = algebraMap Γ(S, ⊤) B a :=
      (IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply Γ(S, ⊤) Γ(X, ⊤) B a).symm
    rw [hgen]
    exact Ideal.map_algebraMap_tensorProduct_eq_span_of_map_eq_span
      (A := Γ(X, ⊤)) _ a (blowup_idealMap_eq_span _ a ha.out)
  exact preimage_exceptionalPreimage_eq_principalZeroLocus f ℐ (CommRingCat.of B)
    (blowUpQuotientBaseChangeChart f ℐ a) (algebraMap Γ(S, ⊤) B) _ hbase hI

/-- **Every point of the blowup of an affine scheme lies in one of the charts in the quotient
model.** This is `Stacks.Blowup.exists_blowUpQuotientChart_preimage` at the affine open `⊤`,
carried along the comparison of the two constructions of the blowup.

Together with `Stacks.StrictTransform.blowUpQuotientBaseChangeChart_snd` it is what makes the
universally quantified conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 0810] say something at every point of the
blown-up base: the chart of the base change over this chart lies over it. -/
public theorem exists_blowUpQuotientChartOfIdeal_preimage (s : blowUp ℐ) :
    ∃ r : ℐ.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top S⟩,
      letI : Fact ((r : Γ(S, ⊤)) ∈ ℐ.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top S⟩) := ⟨r.2⟩
      ∃ t : Spec (CommRingCat.of (Blowup (ℐ.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top S⟩) (r : Γ(S, ⊤)))),
        blowUpQuotientChartOfIdeal ℐ (r : Γ(S, ⊤)) t = s := by
  obtain ⟨r, t, ht⟩ := Stacks.Blowup.exists_blowUpQuotientChart_preimage ℐ
    ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top S⟩ ((Stacks.Blowup.blowUpIso ℐ).inv.base s) trivial
  let : Fact ((r : Γ(S, ⊤)) ∈ ℐ.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top S⟩) := ⟨r.2⟩
  refine ⟨r, t, ?_⟩
  have hcancel : ((Stacks.Blowup.blowUpIso ℐ).inv ≫ (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpIso ℐ).hom).base s
      = s := by
    rw [Iso.inv_hom_id]
    rfl
  calc blowUpQuotientChartOfIdeal ℐ (r : Γ(S, ⊤)) t
      = (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpIso ℐ).hom.base
          (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpQuotientChart ℐ ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top S⟩ (r : Γ(S, ⊤)) t) := rfl
    _ = (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpIso ℐ).hom.base ((Stacks.Blowup.blowUpIso ℐ).inv.base s) := by
        rw [ht]
    _ = s := hcancel

end Stacks.StrictTransform

end
